implementationPlan.description:
docs/MEMORY.md.

(1) Under '### Handoff convention', add the lifecycle:
- `task-<id>-handoff` (and QA's `-qa-handoff`) is written while the task is open;
- it is retired at qa_approve, after its reusable facts are folded into topic memories, by archiving or deleting;
- a rejected task keeps it.

(2) Add the `_archive/` convention:
- retired or merged-away memories move to .serena/memories/_archive/<same name>.md;
- .serena/project.yml `ignored_memory_patterns: [_archive/.*]` hides them from list_memories, read_memory and write_memory, and read_file still reads the raw file;
- the wrappers' pre-flight <inbox> name preload scans only the top level.

(3) Under '### Architects', add the `mem:<name>` pointer convention: name the memory in the plan step that needs it, and never cite an _archive/ name. Under '### QA', add a one-line pointer to the retirement rule in docs/roles/qa.md.

(4) In '## Caveats', adjust the no-dedup or no-merging claim only where it conflicts. Merging stays manual, by edit_memory.

This is an edit, not a rewrite: keep every existing section.

